NOTE:PROFESSIONAL PROFILE\n\nCurrent Role:\nInnovations Executive (Research & Development) at Chipkins Puratos. Reports to Nigel Phillips (MD). Member of the Executive Committee.\n\nScope of Responsibility:\n- Research and Development leadership\n- Product innovation pipeline\n- New product development\n- Technical applications and customer solutions\n- Recipe development and optimisation\n- Liaison with Puratos global R&D network and innovation centres\n- Technology transfer from Puratos headquarters\n\nDocumented Activities:\n- October 2022: Hosted InnoFoodAfrica consortium partners at Chipkins Puratos factory in Edenvale\n- Delivered company presentation to international visitors\n- Led facility tour showcasing production and innovation capabilities\n\nBackground:\nFrench name indicates likely connection to Puratos's Belgian/European headquarters. As Innovations Exec\, serves as bridge between Puratos global R&D capabilities and local South African market needs.\n\nKey Working Relationships:\n- Coordinates with Malibongwe Shelle (Operations Exec) on production of new products\n- Works with Lowell Harkoo (Marketing Exec) on market-driven innovation\n- Interfaces with Silindile Mpungose (Procurement Exec) on new ingredient sourcing\n- Works with David Magrobi (Technical Manager Plants) on technical implementation\n\nColleagues (Chipkins Puratos Exco):\n- Nigel Phillips (MD)\n- Lowell Harkoo (Marketing Exec)\n- Rodney Nel (Finance Exec)\n- Malibongwe Shelle (Operations Exec)\n- Nomsa Kganakga (HR Exec)\n- Silindile Mpungose (Procurement Exec)\n\nSources:\n- https://innofoodafrica.eu/2022/11/09/ifa-consortium-partners-visit-to-chipkins-puratos-bakery/\n- https://www.chipkinspuratos.co.za
